  "type": "self",
  "prompt": "The nine-digit number $302{,}586{,}7ab$ is divisible by $72$. Compute $(a, b)$.",
  "image": null,
  "choices": null,
  "answer": "$(6, 8)$",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Divisible by 8 and 9",
    "body": "For divisibility by $8$, the last three digits $\\overline{7ab}$ must be a multiple of $8$: $700 = 8\\cdot87 + 4$, so $\\overline{ab} \\equiv 4 \\pmod 8$: $\\overline{ab} \\in \\{04, 12, 20, 28, 36, 44, 52, 60, 68, 76, 84, 92\\}$. For divisibility by $9$, the digit sum $3+0+2+5+8+6+7+a+b = 31 + a + b$ must be a multiple of $9$, so $a + b = 5$ or $14$. The only candidate is $68$ ($6 + 8 = 14$).\n\n**Answer: $(a, b) = (6, 8)$**"
   }
  ],
